  "question": "R2, rule S refit 1 (left edge), fresh round: does a one-line Text's drop keep its second row only when its new right line's fraction is under 0.5 and the left and right lines' fractions add to under 1? Unseen setups at 1600: the short Text moved 1, 2 or 4 columns right before it is written (left line 3, 4 or 6), widened by its east side to lines 18, 19, 20 or 24. Read at the drop and let go, twice (R1, R2). Gestures Probe, unsaved.",
  "rule": "S refit 1: a one-line Text widened by its east side keeps its rows at the drop when x of its new right grid line has a fractional part under 0.5 px and under 1 minus the fractional part of x of its left grid line; it falls to the rows it needs otherwise; let go always takes the rows it needs. Grid line x at 1600 = 100.125 + (k - 2) * 58.78125. Where the left fraction is under 0.5 it is rule S.",
